WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.180
<v NARRATOR>For forty years, the lamp on
Gull Rock never missed a night.

00:00:05.439 --> 00:00:07.599
<v NARRATOR>Tomorrow, a machine would take
over.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:15.414
<v MAYA>Last entry in the log, Eli. Wind
from the west. Sea, rough.

00:00:17.874 --> 00:00:20.194
<v ELI>Write that the keeper's daughter
refused to go to bed.

00:00:21.515 --> 00:00:23.855
<v MAYA>You were seven the first time you
said that.

00:00:28.866 --> 00:00:30.906
<v ELI>Maya. Nobody comes out here in a
storm.

00:00:32.272 --> 00:00:33.212
<v MAYA>Stay behind me.

00:00:37.739 --> 00:00:39.499
<v NARRATOR>On the step stood an old man,

00:00:39.499 --> 00:00:42.299
soaked to the bone, with a lantern in his
hand.

00:00:43.912 --> 00:00:45.072
<v MAYA>Dad? You rowed out here? In this?

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:50.940
<v NARRATOR>He didn't answer. He climbed the
stairs, and laid his hand on the glass.

00:00:52.235 --> 00:00:55.155
<v ELI>He kept it burning for thirty of
those years.

00:00:57.276 --> 00:00:58.936
<v MAYA>Then he should be the one to put it
out.

00:01:00.531 --> 00:01:05.111
<v NARRATOR>At dawn, the old keeper turned
the key. And for the first time in forty

00:01:05.111 --> 00:01:07.011
years, Gull Rock went dark.
